{
  "summary": "Adds a safeguard in PeerManager to prevent transactions tracked in private broadcast storage from being announced over public peer connections. It introduces a TxAnnounceReason parameter to distinguish transaction relay (received from network peers) from local announcement requests (such as RPC submissions, wallet rebroadcasts, and mempool unbroadcast retries). If a non-relay announcement is initiated for a transaction present in private broadcast storage, PeerManager suppresses the broadcast and removes the transaction from the mempool unbroadcast set.",
  "problem": "Transactions broadcast via private broadcast can inadvertently be announced to public peers if re-triggered locally—such as through submitpackage RPC calls, periodic wallet resends after the transaction is echoed back from the network, GUI PSBT broadcasts, or unbroadcast retry timers. Announcing them to public peers exposes the node as the origin and undermines private broadcast protections.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'During the initial phase of private broadcast implementation there were unforeseen instances when a private transaction could get broadcast non-privately (see #35032 #35319 #35410 #36309 #36312 #36277 #36330)... Add a general, extra safeguard: whenever there is a transaction broadcast request, check if the given transaction has been previously broadcast privately, and if so, refuse to broadcast non-privately.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
   "depends_on": [
    "#36477"
   ],
   "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Includes commits and diff from underlying PR #36477, which updates private broadcast queue retention and RPC metadata.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Tests in test/functional/p2p_private_broadcast_then_public.py were split into separate commits for the submitpackage and wallet resend scenarios.",
  "card": "Adds a safeguard in PeerManager to block unintended public announcements of transactions previously sent via private broadcast. Subsystems like submitpackage, periodic wallet rebroadcast, and mempool unbroadcast retries could otherwise announce these transactions across public peer connections, leaking origin identity. PeerManager::InitiateTxBroadcastToAll distinguishes relay from requested announcements, dropping public announcements and clearing unbroadcast retries for transactions tracked in private broadcast storage. It depends on base PR #36477 to keep finished private broadcast records in memory so they can be matched.",
